From 4eb168663cb70135235836a4ebe55c93383fd38b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrew Youll <andrewyoull86@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 22:57:31 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] yadif arm: NEON line filter for 32-bit ARM (8 bits a sample)

Bit-exact with filter_line_c: eight pixels an iteration, sums and scores
in 16 bits, the averages with vhadd. Byte-element loads and stores only,
so it needs no alignment (RISC OS traps unaligned wider accesses). Like
the x86 versions it may read 2 bytes and write up to 7 pixels past w,
which vf_yadif.c leaves room for (filter_edges writes the right-hand
pixels afterwards).
---
 libavfilter/arm/Makefile        |   3 +
 libavfilter/arm/vf_yadif_init.c |  36 ++++++
 libavfilter/arm/vf_yadif_neon.S | 198 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 libavfilter/vf_yadif.c          |   3 +
 libavfilter/yadif.h             |   1 +
 5 files changed, 241 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 libavfilter/arm/Makefile
 create mode 100644 libavfilter/arm/vf_yadif_init.c
 create mode 100644 libavfilter/arm/vf_yadif_neon.S

diff --git a/libavfilter/arm/Makefile b/libavfilter/arm/Makefile
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..63b3585
--- /dev/null
+++ b/libavfilter/arm/Makefile
@@ -0,0 +1,3 @@
+OBJS-$(CONFIG_YADIF_FILTER)                  += arm/vf_yadif_init.o
+
+NEON-OBJS-$(CONFIG_YADIF_FILTER)             += arm/vf_yadif_neon.o
diff --git a/libavfilter/arm/vf_yadif_init.c b/libavfilter/arm/vf_yadif_init.c
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..a9663c8
--- /dev/null
+++ b/libavfilter/arm/vf_yadif_init.c
@@ -0,0 +1,36 @@
